// Windows resource script for the host binary. GENERATED into the build tree
// by native/src/host/CMakeLists.txt (configure_file), so the icon path is
// absolute and does not depend on the working directory of rc.exe.
//
// Two entries, deliberately, both pointing at the same .ico:
//
//   1          Explorer, the taskbar and Alt-Tab take the icon group with the
//              lowest ordinal ID.
//   GLFW_ICON  the window's own icon. GLFW looks up this exact name on the
//              running module (native/third_party/glfw/src/win32_window.c:
//              LoadImageW(GetModuleHandleW(NULL), L"GLFW_ICON", ...)) and
//              falls back to IDI_APPLICATION -- the generic blank page -- if
//              it is missing. Without this line the title bar keeps that
//              placeholder even when Explorer shows the right icon.
//
// The data is embedded twice (about 50 KB each, against a multi-megabyte
// binary). That buys independence: neither consumer's lookup rule depends on
// the other's, and no code has to run to set the window icon.
//
// No #include <windows.h> here on purpose: nothing below needs a macro from
// it, and leaving it out means rc.exe needs no INCLUDE path to succeed.

1 ICON "@DAUNTLESS_ICON_PATH@"
GLFW_ICON ICON "@DAUNTLESS_ICON_PATH@"
